## Portable rerun

From the repository root, using Python3.13 or a compatible modern Python:

```sh
python computation/reproduce.py --quick --workdir /tmp/cm-lm-check
```

This copies only the new independent checker to a fresh work directory and reads the preserved benchmark raw CSV. It does not modify source snapshots or recorded output. The core checker uses the Python standard library only. A second independent script checks the explicit oracle-interface qualification.

For the supplied mathematical implementations, first create an environment with the packages in [requirements.txt](requirements.txt), then run:

```sh
python computation/reproduce.py --all --historical --workdir /tmp/cm-lm-full
```

`--all` reruns explicit stages, not the interrupted aggregate driver. `--historical` adds the four unchanged embedded historical test suites in separate interpreters. The runner copies all chosen source snapshots, records each command/return code/duration, stops on failures, and puts outputs under the chosen work directory. A work directory that already exists is rejected to avoid overwriting prior results. The runner does not install packages, contact services, launch a timing campaign, or modify the repository. A subprocess timeout is logged as such, never PASS.

For exact-original performance campaign commands, consult the benchmark snapshot's protocol; `--all` only audits its stored raw observations and executes correctness tests. Copying the original Python timing numbers into a new environment does not reproduce those timings.

